+# Nightly Launchd Job Review & Diagnosis
+
+## Summary of Root Causes
+
+The nightly launchd job (`com.vk.nightly-review`) ran and failed, but never reported any notifications (neither success nor failure) to Telegram due to two distinct causes:
+
+1. **Why `claude` failed (`Not logged in · Please run /login`)**:
+   - Claude Code (`claude`) failed with exit code 1 because it was not authenticated or could not access the required authentication credentials in the headless launchd environment.
+
+2. **Why no failure notification was sent over Telegram (`read-only variable: status`)**:
+   - In [nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24), line 19 attempted to capture the exit status with `status=$?`.
+   - In zsh, `status` is a special built-in read-only variable aliased to `$?`. Attempting to assign to `status` (`status=$?`) throws a fatal error:
+     ```text
+     zsh: read-only variable: status
+     ```
+   - Because `status=$?` caused the zsh script to abort immediately, execution never reached lines 21–23 where `bin/notify.sh` would have been called to send the failure alert to Telegram.
+
+---
+
+## Fix Applied
+
+- In [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19-L23), replaced the assignment to the read-only variable `status` with `exit_code`:
+  ```zsh
+  claude -p "$PROMPT" --output-format text > "$OUT"
+  exit_code=$?
+
+  if [ $exit_code -ne 0 ]; then
+    "$NOTIFY" "nightly review FAILED (exit $exit_code), see $OUT"
+    exit $exit_code
+  fi
+  ```
+  Now, if `claude` (or any command) fails, the error handler properly executes and sends a failure notification via Telegram.
+
+## Recommendations for Claude Authentication in Launchd
+
+To fix the underlying `claude` execution error:
+- Authenticate Claude or provide the necessary API key environment variable (such as `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) within [Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist) under `<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>`, or ensure Claude Code's login credentials directory (`~/.claude` or config file) is accessible by the launchd job environment.
